  "body": "Here's a working demo:\r\n\r\nhttps://codepen.io/trusktr/pen/gOMjELg\r\n\r\nIn the following demo, `event.preventDefault()` is called in a `pointerdown` event, and that (seemingly inexplicably from an end user perspective) breaks `mouseup` events:\r\n\r\nhttps://codepen.io/trusktr/pen/GRqBeWr\r\n\r\nThis has been a source of difficult-to-track bugs in an application I'm working on. It really isn't intuitive that one set of events (`pointer*` events) has such an effect on an unrelated set of events (`mouse*` events).\r\n\r\nAnd even if `pointer` and `mouse` events _are_ grouped together, it is not at all clear why `event.preventDefault()` within `*down` event handlers should stop `*up` event handlers from firing.\r\n\r\nFurthermore, `click` events are not damaged while `mouseup` events are, leading to further unintuitive and confusing behavior.\r\n\r\nThe following is the same demo with `pointerdown` calling `event.preventDefault()`, but the demo works because it uses `click` instead of `mouseup`:\r\n\r\nhttps://codepen.io/trusktr/pen/VwjBRXj",
